You are analyzing a 3x3 grid of frames sampled evenly across a video.

## Task

Classify the video's visible setup — `scene`:

- `"interview"`: two people in conversation, typically seated facing each other in one static wide shot;
- `"presentation"`: one speaker presenting — a stage, a podium, or a single talking head;
- `"other"`: anything else (no people, montage, screen recording, b-roll only).

Judge the setup by what MOST of the frames show: a brief cutaway (audience shot, b-roll insert) in a few frames never changes the setup. People count is not your job — a separate deterministic pass measures it; you only read the scene.

## Output format

Output only valid JSON:

{
  "scene": "interview" | "presentation" | "other",
  "confidence": "high" | "low"
}

Set `confidence` to `"low"` when the grid is genuinely ambiguous (people partly out of frame, heavy occlusion, mixed setups). Output JSON only — no markdown, no commentary.
